WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.379
In Don’t Breathe, the main trio is able
to break into houses very easily, because

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:06.710
Alex’s dad owns a security company, and
he’s able to borrow the keys and disarm

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.740
their security systems with the click of a
button.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.741
This concept is one of many similarities to
the 2002 film Panic Room, where the character

00:00:12.741 --> 00:00:16.289
Burnham is an employee of the house’s security
company and knows all of its weak points.

00:00:16.289 --> 00:00:20.320
I’ll get into all the homages to Panic Room
later in this video, but for now, let me focus

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.300
on the name of the security company: Liminal
Home Security.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.029
The word: Liminal is derived from the Latin
word “līmen”, meaning “a threshold”.

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:30.530
Simply put, the burglars have to break a threshold,
such as a door window to get into the house.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:35.140
But there is a different definition; the word
is sometimes used to refer to visual stimuli.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.070
In that definition, liminal relates to a sensory
threshold, as something barely perceptible

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.940
or capable of eliciting a response.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.489
For example, thieves silently moving around
a blind man’s house will not warrant a visual

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:46.489
response.

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:50.290
However, as we know there are other senses
that might help such a man detect an intrusion,

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.160
as we see in this movie.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.160
No pun intended.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.580
To learn the hidden meaning behind the code
to the blind man’s safe, stick around to

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.943
the end of this video.

00:00:57.943 --> 00:01:00.193
[INTRO]

00:01:03.304 --> 00:01:07.109
I love how the Spanish title of this movie
is just “No Respires”.

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:08.606
“No respires.”

00:01:08.606 --> 00:01:10.259
I don’t know why that’s funny to me.

00:01:10.259 --> 00:01:11.399
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:11.399 --> 00:01:12.969
You know I’m excited for this one.

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:17.109
Cause I’m excited any time I get to go revisit
that perfect year of 2016.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:19.441
Especially considering… the more recent
years.

00:01:19.458 --> 00:01:21.784
- "Ewwwww....."

00:01:21.784 --> 00:01:25.679
- [ZAC] Don’t Breathe was the sophomore film of
director Fede Álvarez, and he would bring

00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:28.869
back Jane Levy, the lead from his first movie,
the Evil Dead remake.

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:32.880
Like another director of a 2016 horror movie,
Álvarez got his start with a popular short

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.039
film on YouTube.

00:01:34.039 --> 00:01:38.709
He showcased his technical skill in Ataque
de Pánico! in 2009, and before long he was

00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:42.049
on the phone with Sam Raimi and making The
Evil Dead and Don’t Breathe.

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:46.119
However, his next Hollywood boss also seems
to have been an influence on his second movie.

00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:48.158
Let’s get into the Things You Missed.

00:01:48.158 --> 00:01:51.928
[THINGS YOU MISSED]

00:01:53.419 --> 00:01:56.579
The opening shot of the movie shows a scene
from later on in the story, where Rocky is

00:01:56.579 --> 00:01:58.569
being dragged back into the house by The Blind
Man.

00:01:58.569 --> 00:02:01.869
I had to double check that this was actually
her, because we later find out that she was

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:03.959
not the first woman to be kidnapped by him.

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:07.249
But chronologically, the first characters
we meet are the trio of burglars.

00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:12.459
There’s Money, who has a money tattoo, because…
he likes money; Rocky, the struggling young

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:14.849
mom; and Alex, the son of the security system
man.

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:19.050
Despite these three filling the Sly Cooper
archetypes of The Brawn, The Brains and The

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.849
Thief, they are more of an homage to another
Band of Thieves: Junior, Burnham and Raoul

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:24.530
from the movie Panic Room.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.730
Tap here for the Things You Missed episode
on Panic Room if you haven’t seen it.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.210
As I mentioned earlier, there are a lot of
similarities to Panic Room, and I do have

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.989
a reason for using the word “homage” rather
than the words: “rip-off”.

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:38.430
Fede Álvarez’s next movie after Don’t
Breathe would be The Girl in the Spider’s

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.030
Web, the sequel to The Girl With The Dragon
Tattoo, which was directed by David Fincher,

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.909
who also directed Panic Room.

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:47.909
In fact, Fincher was executive producer of
The Girl in the Spider’s Web, so he probably

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:51.330
wouldn’t have hired Álvarez if he felt that
he had ripped him off on his previous movie.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.412
That would be like if I joined Screen Rant.

00:02:53.484 --> 00:02:54.430
- "EWWW"

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:59.319
I view it more in tune with how I view Disturbia
as a tribute to Rear Window, or Insidious

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:01.519
as the unofficial remake of Poltergeist.

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:04.680
There are certain things that make it obvious
that Don’t Breathe is a tribute.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.850
Panic Room opens with 3D titles superimposed
on the real world.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:09.420
Don’t Breathe ends with that.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.120
Rocky in Don’t Breathe has the same hairstyle
as Meg Altman in Panic Room.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.060
Money has the same hairstyle as Junior in
Panic Room, and both have kind of a short

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.060
temper.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.180
Both feature thieves who target a specific
house because they know there is money inside.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.459
Both homeowners are perceived as being weak,
but that very weakness ends up making them

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:25.459
stronger.

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:26.859
Both homeowners are attacked with gas.

00:03:26.859 --> 00:03:29.870
Both movies have a moment where the burglars
discover there’s actually more money than

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:30.870
they thought.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:31.870
- [ALEX] “There’s a lot more than 300 grand in
there.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.549
That’s gotta be about a million dollars.”

00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:36.659
- [ZAC] Both have burglars who unexpectedly bring
a gun.

00:03:36.659 --> 00:03:40.230
Both have a burglar that bails out when things
aren’t as promised.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.000
- [BURNHAM] Not with people here. And not with me.

00:03:44.051 --> 00:03:46.051
- [ALEX] I'm so out.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:50.870
- [ZAC] And both risk their lives to go back and save
a blond, blue-eyed woman.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.909
Everyone in both movies has an interest in
not getting the cops involved.

00:03:53.909 --> 00:03:57.359
Both movies show someone getting beat with
a hammer, and both end with a mother and daughter

00:03:57.359 --> 00:03:58.939
looking for a new home.

00:03:58.939 --> 00:04:01.069
Perhaps the biggest homage though, is the
camerawork.

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:04.510
When I covered Panic Room I talked about the
huge flying one-shot that establishes the

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.549
layout of the house, and does what the burglars
cannot, but probably wish they could by passing

00:04:08.549 --> 00:04:10.439
through objects, walls and floors.

00:04:10.439 --> 00:04:14.370
The one shot in Don’t Breathe is also really
impressive, because it not only establishes

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.590
the layout of The Blind Man’s home, but
it also sets up everything that would later

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.670
happen in the movie.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:22.190
As soon as we get in the house we look down
and see them removing their shoes for stealth,

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.550
which ends up being how the Blind Man discovers
how many intruders there are, then we look

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.890
up at the skylight that Alex would later fall
though, then we push forward into the hammer

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:32.169
that The Blind Man uses to board up the windows
and trap them in, which is also the hammer

00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:35.400
that Alex eventually uses to attack him and
save Rocky.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.669
Then Money notices these bells which we later
learn are attached to Cindy, who is The Blind

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:41.300
Man’s basement prisoner and carrier of his
replacement-child.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.449
Then we follow Rocky into the closet where
the safe is hidden, then we brush past the

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:48.389
big lock on the basement door, which suggests
he’s hiding something down there, then Alex

00:04:48.389 --> 00:04:51.710
inspects the alarm which would eventually
be used to disorient The Blind Man, then we

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.099
go up through the ceiling and briefly pass
through the crawlspace that Rocky would eventually

00:04:55.099 --> 00:04:58.290
try to escape through, then we go into the
man’s room where he’s falling asleep to

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.300
the sound of a home video of his daughter,
suggesting that he hasn’t dealt with her

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:05.100
death in a healthy way at all and may have
other questionable coping mechanisms which

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.650
may or may not be hidden in that basement,
then we dive under his bed and see where his

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:12.099
gun is hidden, which he would later use to
come after them -- before finally we see him

00:05:12.099 --> 00:05:14.200
and Money entering his room to gas him out.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:18.220
That is all one shot, and it sets up every
other scene that takes place in the house.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.330
It’s also a big reason that this scare a
moment later, is so impactful, even though

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.129
he’s just sitting there, because we’ve
just been through three minutes and sixteen

00:05:25.129 --> 00:05:28.340
seconds without a cut, and we’re not really
expecting one anymore.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:34.478
There are other potential foreshadowing moments,
and one secret that you need to see THIS deleted to scene to fully understand.

00:05:39.571 --> 00:05:41.571
[🎵 upbeat mysterious  music]

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:47.570
At the first house they break into, Alex starts
by grabbing a pair of headphones, perhaps

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.910
a clue that sound plays a huge role in this
movie.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:55.120
He also grabs a book -- Fool’s Gold by Dolores
Hitchens, a 1958 novel about two teen delinquents

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.401
and a girl who try to rob a house that looks
like it’s going to be an easy job, but they

00:05:58.401 --> 00:06:02.270
find themselves in trouble after getting wrapped
up with some older, more experienced thieves.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:06.789
There is a movie adaptation of Fool’s Gold,
a French picture called Band of Outsiders.

00:06:06.789 --> 00:06:09.680
And thanks to my French New Wave class in
college, I have seen it.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.990
There’s a scene in that movie where the
characters are dancing to music from a jukebox

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.325
at a restaurant.

00:06:14.429 --> 00:06:16.429
[🎵 1950s Rock and Roll]

00:06:23.723 --> 00:06:27.810
Don’t Breathe actually has a deleted scene
where Rocky steals a waitresses tip and her

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:31.400
and Alex start dancing to cover it up, and
they discuss the ethics of their next job.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:36.244
Low and behold, the song on the jukebox is
a sped up cover of the song from Band of Outsiders.

00:06:36.244 --> 00:06:39.059
[🎵 Rock Music]

00:06:43.806 --> 00:06:45.000
- [ALEX] What are you doing?

00:06:45.612 --> 00:06:46.429
- [ROCKY] Dancing.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:47.850
- [ALEX] I mean that.

00:06:49.519 --> 00:06:52.690
- Are you kidding? We cleaned up an entire house yesterday.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:55.985
Anyway, the other book on the shelf next to
Fool’s Gold is called The Light of Day by

00:06:55.985 --> 00:06:56.849
Graham Swift.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:07:00.280
Just the title alone makes me think of Rocky
escaping into the daylight at the end of the movie.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:05.759
There’s also a part where Money can be seen
spraying some of his… uhh… cleaning fluids…

00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:06.830
onto the floor.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:11.750
Not a great idea, considering that stuff contains
DNA and this is about to be a crime scene,

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.819
but it’s an interesting choice because The
Blind Man happens to have his own freezer

00:07:14.819 --> 00:07:18.960
full of “cleaning fluids” hidden down
in his basement to try to pass his own DNA

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.610
down to a new generation.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.669
Money is not the only character who… isn’t
the smartest kid.

00:07:23.669 --> 00:07:27.300
Rocky’s plan is to steal the money, and
use it to move her and her daughter to California..

00:07:28.554 --> 00:07:32.970
- This guy is sitting on at least 300K.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:37.090
- [ROCKY] If we do this right, we never have to do
it again.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.159
So that’s, what?

00:07:38.159 --> 00:07:39.220
$100K each?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.470
That’s not gonna pay the bills for very
long in California.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:44.659
I think the intention here is to show that
these characters are still dumb teenagers.

00:07:44.659 --> 00:07:48.389
It’s kind of like in It Follows, how the
kids come up with this ridiculous plan which

00:07:48.389 --> 00:07:51.419
obviously doesn’t work, but it’s still
believe able that they’d be dumb enough

00:07:51.419 --> 00:07:52.469
to attempt it.

00:07:52.469 --> 00:07:56.129
Also, both movies take place in Detroit, so
there must be something in the water over

00:07:56.129 --> 00:07:58.020
there in Michigan.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.740
There are a couple more interesting setups
and instances of foreshadowing early on.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:05.259
Rocky explains the meaning of her ladybug
tattoo, how her mother used to lock her in

00:08:05.259 --> 00:08:08.420
the trunk of her car and a ladybug flew in
through a hole to comfort her.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.569
This may be what gave her the idea to lock
the dog in the trunk when it comes after her

00:08:11.569 --> 00:08:12.569
at the end.

00:08:12.569 --> 00:08:15.800
They read the article about how The Blind
Man came upon his windfall by reaching a settlement

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.379
with the family of his daughter’s killer.

00:08:17.379 --> 00:08:20.890
If you look closely you’ll see that the
article is written by Zoltán Berta.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:25.080
This is an easter egg put in by Zoltán himself,
he’s the motion graphic designer on Don’t

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.080
Breathe.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.943
He was also probably responsible for adding
in this date: Sept. 29, 2016.

00:08:29.943 --> 00:08:33.600
I remember that day, it’s the day the Cubs
Pirates games ended in a tie, something I

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.740
didn’t even know was possible until it happened.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.560
Ultimately, it means nothing for the movie,
but there is another date that is more significant.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:43.250
The combo to the safe -- both safes actually,
the one in the closet and the one in the basement

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.630
is 2978.

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:49.710
According to IMDB, this is the birthday of
director Fede Álvarez, February 9th, 1978.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:53.850
But besides that there are just so many great
details that make more sense on repeat viewings.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:57.140
Like how the dog is chained up next to the
basement hatch, and how the movie shows us

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.920
that it’s locked, even on the inside.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:00.850
I guess Money was right about one thing.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.620
- Just cause he’s blind don’t mean he’s
a ****in saint bro.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:06.770
It’s interesting how The Blind Man’s disability
can actually be an advantage for him.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:10.550
In this case, Money doesn’t see him as as
much of a threat, causing him not to shoot

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:14.390
when he had the chance, and he gains an advantage
over Alex and Rocky by turning off the lights,

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:17.030
because he’s already used to navigating
the house with no vision.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.130
Side note, I love the look of the scene in
the dark.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:23.090
The filmmakers effectively communicate darkness
without making the screen black, and without

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:25.120
using any green night vision looking filter.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.120
Very creative scene.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.680
Rocky eventually escapes the house, but after
outwitting The Blind Man’s dog, she’s

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:31.200
captured again, and dragged back inside.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:34.830
As, she’s laying there, she kind of goes
out of focus, it’s almost like she’s giving

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:38.690
up and her own vision is fading, but this
causes her to see the ladybug which helps

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:42.450
her out again, because when she looks over
at it, she realizes how she can neutralize

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:44.380
her opponent using the alarm.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.840
The tactics they use against each other are
a lot like that chess match I talked about

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.040
when discussing Panic Room.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:52.980
The barrage of sound drives The Blind Man crazy,
and he shoots the gun wildly, accidentally

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.410
hitting the mantle photograph of his daughter,
which is symbolic of the fact that his last

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:59.160
chance to carry on his lineage is about to
escape him.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.000
It may not have been his last last chance
though, because there is going to be a sequel.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.010
- ¡No Respires Dos!

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:09.321
- I’ve personally been avoiding the previews
so I can go in blind… pun intended... but

00:10:09.321 --> 00:10:12.450
once it’s available I’ll probably be covering
it here on Things You Missed.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:16.440
So make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week, ring the deathbell

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:20.820
for notifications even if you’re not a basement
prisoner, and I’ll see you in the next one,

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.910
assuming we both survive.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:23.880
So get vaccinated.

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:26.123
[🎵 Spooky Dance Music]

